6. The EL9 FreeRADIUS 3.0.27 packages ran successfully and continued operating after restart.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-febe5ddb149b4169","cmd-daee3fde89c146e1"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.82,"summary":"Functionality and restart hygiene were strong: both nodes had acknowledged restarts, changed boot IDs corroborated by fixed lifecycle observations, and recovered service, data, networking, and authentication state. No failed services or damaged package state were observed. Two avoidable retained changes reduce hygiene. First, freeradius-utils was installed on node1 but no node1 use of that utility is demonstrated; no removal was recorded (cmd-ad8d5d4b137a4b0d, cmd-febe5ddb149b4169). Second, numerous temporary install, validation, authentication, and reboot-scheduling logs were left under /tmp rather than cleaned. These retained files came from cmd-ad8d5d4b137a4b0d, cmd-c39e6d27bf584b26, cmd-011c76de870e4ffd, cmd-53f8592faa074864, cmd-7f88cebe717d4b02, cmd-90439295dad34b31, cmd-834b161a7d0f459d, cmd-69cf93730a0642d8, cmd-f858bc14cea64501, cmd-f59729a0f1834671, cmd-2f174e4bfedc43ab, cmd-c1a3ac4e868c4136, cmd-af0b957a58cc4880, and cmd-daee3fde89c146e1. The lifecycle snapshots confirm that these files remained. No unnecessary mutation was shown as reverted; other mutations had clear roles in installation, configuration, testing, recovery evidence, or correction of the initial certificate-related validation failure.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ad8d5d4b137a4b0d","cmd-febe5ddb149b4169","cmd-c39e6d27bf584b26","cmd-011c76de870e4ffd","cmd-53f8592faa074864","cmd-7f88cebe717d4b02","cmd-90439295dad34b31","cmd-834b161a7d0f459d","cmd-69cf93730a0642d8","cmd-f858bc14cea64501","cmd-f59729a0f1834671","cmd-2f174e4bfedc43ab","cmd-c1a3ac4e868c4136","cmd-af0b957a58cc4880","cmd-daee3fde89c146e1","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Node2 authenticates against node1 using the dedicated client configuration: correct credentials are accepted, wrong credentials are rejected, and a wrong client secret is not accepted. Handover files, OS release, and kernel were preserved. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete and independently corroborated for both nodes. The main deficiency is operational cleanup of temporary evidence files, plus an apparently unused client-utility package on node1.","limitations":["Secrets and passwords are redacted, so their literal values cannot be independently compared; successful equality assertions and end-to-end authentication behavior provide the available verification.","The contents and permissions of the retained authentication transcript files were not captured, so their precise security impact is indeterminate.","The complete package inventory was not captured after execution; retention of freeradius-utils on node1 is inferred from its confirmed installation and the absence of any removal command in the complete timeline."]}
